    "title": "📅 Wheeler's Park historic marker unveiling in Harrington",
    "text": "1 days ago 📅 New historical marker ceremony for Wheeler’s Park\nA new State of Delaware Historical Marker honoring Wheeler’s Park will be unveiled on Thursday, October 1, 2026, at 1:00 p.m. at 428 Harrington Avenue in Harrington .\nWheeler’s Park, opened in 1948 by William A. Wheeler , was once known as the “Disneyland of Harrington.” It featured playgrounds, pony rides, a miniature railroad, nature trails , and hosted church picnics and company events for Dover Air Force Base and businesses across Kent and Sussex counties until it closed in 1977 .\nThe ceremony will include Harrington community members , local and state leaders , and representatives from the Delaware Public Archives , which runs the State Historical Markers Program .\nFor more on the Delaware Public Archives and its events, visit archives.delaware.gov and follow them on Facebook and Instagram .\nMore Info: Unveiling of New State Historical Marker Honoring ...\nThis article includes content summarized and organized with AI tools, which can make mistakes. Learn more.\n1",
    "summary": "1 days ago 📅 New historical marker ceremony for Wheeler’s Park A new State of Delaware Historical Marker honoring Wheeler’s Park will be unveiled on Thursday, October 1, 2026, at 1:00 p.m. at 428 Harrington Avenue in Harrington . Wheeler’s Park, opened in 1948 by William A. Wheeler , was once known as the “Disneyland of Harrington.” It featured playgrounds, pony rides, a miniature railroad, nature trails , and hosted church picnics and company events for Dover Air Force Base and businesses across Kent and Sussex counties until it closed in 1977 .",
